# dsh command reference

Generated from the command tree by `dsh catalog commands`. Do not edit by hand.

## dsh

```text
Usage: dsh [options] [profile|command...]

The DeepSeek harness: launch a profile or run a fixed command.

Launcher options come before the profile or command name. Every word after a
profile name, or after --profile <name>, belongs to the profile's app, --help included.

Commands:
  help        Show the help of a command or a profile
  version     Print the version of this build
  catalog     Print the generated catalogs of this build
  completion  Print a shell completion script

Profiles:
  web          Start the host and open the web UI
  headless     Run one task without a UI and print the answer
  sdk          Serve the SDK protocol on standard input and output
  sdk-minimal  Serve the SDK protocol with the minimal agent preset
  acp          Serve the Agent Client Protocol on standard input and output

Options:
      --home <dir>      Harness home (default $DSH_HOME, then ~/.dsh)
      --profile <name>  Profile to launch; every later word goes to its app
      --layer <file>    Add a config layer above the user layer (repeatable)
      --safe            Start with optional bundles and plugins off
  -V, --version         Print the version and exit
  -h, --help            Show this help

Examples:
  dsh web
      Start the host and open the web UI
  dsh --home ./h --layer extra.yml headless "run the tests" --json
  dsh --profile sdk
      How programs start the SDK protocol
```

## dsh help

```text
Usage: dsh help [options] [command...]

Show the help of a command or a profile

Arguments:
  command  A command path or a profile name

Options:
  -h, --help  Show this help

Examples:
  dsh help catalog commands
```

## dsh version

```text
Usage: dsh version [options]

Print the version of this build

Options:
      --json  Print the result as one JSON value
  -h, --help  Show this help
```

## dsh catalog

```text
Usage: dsh catalog [options] <command>...

Print the generated catalogs of this build

Commands:
  commands  Print the command reference

Options:
  -h, --help  Show this help
```

## dsh catalog commands

```text
Usage: dsh catalog commands [options]

Print the command reference

Options:
      --json  Print the result as one JSON value
  -h, --help  Show this help

Examples:
  dsh catalog commands > reference.md
```

## dsh completion

```text
Usage: dsh completion [options] <shell>

Print a shell completion script

Arguments:
  shell  bash, zsh, fish, powershell

Options:
  -h, --help  Show this help

Examples:
  dsh completion bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/dsh
  dsh completion powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression
```

## Profiles

| Profile | Bundles | Summary |
|---|---|---|
| `web` | core, web | Start the host and open the web UI |
| `headless` | core, headless | Run one task without a UI and print the answer |
| `sdk` | core, sdk | Serve the SDK protocol on standard input and output |
| `sdk-minimal` | core, minimal, sdk | Serve the SDK protocol with the minimal agent preset |
| `acp` | core, acp | Serve the Agent Client Protocol on standard input and output |

## Exit statuses

| Status | Name | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | ok | Success; also help and version |
| 1 | failed | The thing asked for ran and failed |
| 3 | denied | Denied by policy, a guard or a person |
| 4 | unavailable | Unavailable: no host, no endpoint, a capability that is missing |
| 5 | invalid | Invalid input or not found: an unknown session, tool or profile |
| 6 | busy | Busy or conflict |
| 7 | limit | A limit or a timeout ended the work |
| 8 | cancelled | Cancelled, or the outcome is unknown |
| 64 | usage | Usage error: unknown command or flag, a broken rule between flags, a missing argument |
| 70 | fatal | Fatal error with a report written |
| 78 | config | The configuration cannot be composed, or a required entry failed to load |
| 124 | forced | Forced exit: the exit deadline passed during shutdown |
| 125 | stalled | A stdio client stopped reading |
| 130 | interrupted | Interrupted by Ctrl-C |

## Reserved words

No profile may be called: `__complete`, `__completeNoDesc`, `catalog`, `completion`, `help`, `sandbox-launch`, `ssh-helper`, `version`.
